    <div class="admin-page-heading"><div><p class="admin-eyebrow">Workspace help</p><h1>Father's Heart user guide</h1><p>Follow the steps below to navigate the workspace, manage records and protect private information. Screens and actions depend on your permissions.</p></div>@if(!($standalone ?? false))<a class="admin-primary-link" href="{{ route('user-guide.download') }}">Download guide</a>@endif</div>
    <section class="admin-form-card admin-form-section"><h2>On this page</h2><nav class="guide-nav" aria-label="Guide sections"><a href="#guide-signin">Sign in</a><a href="#guide-dashboard">Dashboard</a><a href="#guide-people">People</a><a href="#guide-assessments">Assessments</a><a href="#guide-media">Media &amp; consent</a><a href="#guide-distributions">Distributions</a><a href="#guide-inventory">Inventory</a><a href="#guide-accounts">Staff &amp; roles</a><a href="#guide-reports">Filters &amp; exports</a><a href="#guide-therapy">Children’s therapy</a></nav></section>
    <section id="guide-signin" class="admin-form-card admin-form-section"><h2>1. Sign in and request access</h2><p>Enter your staff email and password, then select Sign in. Use Forgot password if you need a reset. If you do not have an account, choose Request staff registration, enter your details and submit your request. A super administrator must approve it before you can sign in.</p>@include('admin.guide-screenshot', ['file' => 'loginpage.png', 'alt' => 'Father’s Heart sign-in page', 'caption' => 'Sign-in screen'])<p>On the request form, choose your requested role; an administrator can change it before approval. The system does not automatically notify applicants, so contact your administrator about the decision.</p>@include('admin.guide-screenshot', ['file' => 'registrationpage.png', 'alt' => 'Staff access request form', 'caption' => 'Request staff access'])</section>
    <section id="guide-dashboard" class="admin-form-card admin-form-section"><h2>2. Use the dashboard</h2><p>After signing in, use the reporting-month filter to review registrations, ongoing assessments, upcoming events and inventory movements. Open a section in the sidebar to find its pages. The information and actions shown depend on your assigned permissions.</p>@include('admin.guide-screenshot', ['file' => 'main dashboard.png', 'alt' => 'Ministry dashboard with sidebar and monthly statistics', 'caption' => 'Dashboard and workspace navigation'])</section>
    <section id="guide-people" class="admin-form-card admin-form-section"><h2>3. Register a person</h2><p>Open People &amp; care → People. Search by name, phone or person number before selecting Register person. Enter the available details and save. Shared phone numbers can belong to different people, so review any duplicate warning before confirming. Use the filters and export controls where your role permits them.</p>@include('admin.guide-screenshot', ['file' => 'peopleregistrypage.png', 'alt' => 'People registry with search filters and record actions', 'caption' => 'People registry: search, registration and record actions'])<p>Historical entries may represent the same person; they are not merged automatically. Registration-date filters exclude historical entries whose original date is unknown.</p></section>
    <section id="guide-assessments" class="admin-form-card admin-form-section"><h2>4. Complete an assessment</h2><p>From a person’s record, select Add assessment. Enter the available information, select a distribution event and location when appropriate, and use either step-by-step or full-form view. The intake code is generated automatically. The final section records a separate consent decision when the signed form is available.</p><p>A device considered is not proof of handover. Historical device and date values are unverified; an old date may reflect a later edit.</p></section>
    <section id="guide-media" class="admin-form-card admin-form-section"><h2>5. Photos, testimony videos and consent</h2><p>On a supported device, use the camera or upload controls to add assessment photos. Authorized staff can open People &amp; care → Testimony videos to upload and privately view MP4, WebM or MOV recordings. Historical photo matches are unverified and can belong to another person if filenames were reused.</p><p>Media remains private and is not automatically published. A photo or video is not consent: verify the appropriate signed form and guardian permission where applicable before external sharing.</p></section>
    <section id="guide-distributions" class="admin-form-card admin-form-section"><h2>6. Manage distribution events</h2><p>Open Distributions → Distribution events to plan, view or update an event. Link the event to assessments to organize recipients. Historical event names, dates and locations are unverified; review them before treating them as confirmed.</p>@include('admin.guide-screenshot', ['file' => 'distributionpage.png', 'alt' => 'Distribution events table and its actions', 'caption' => 'Distribution events and available actions'])</section>
    <section id="guide-inventory" class="admin-form-card admin-form-section"><h2>7. Manage inventory</h2><p>Open Inventory → Stock management to add, view or edit an item. Record an opening balance only after a physical stock count has been reviewed and approved. Thereafter record stock in and out with the date and an optional reference. Items with stock history cannot be deleted, and units cannot be changed after stock is recorded.</p>@include('admin.guide-screenshot', ['file' => 'inventory.png', 'alt' => 'Inventory page with items and opening count actions', 'caption' => 'Stock management and opening counts'])<p>Historical stock contains old snapshots, not verified current balances. Consult the separate Historical stock page without treating those references as current stock.</p></section>
    <section id="guide-accounts" class="admin-form-card admin-form-section"><h2>8. Staff, roles and permissions</h2><p>Under User management, authorized staff can manage accounts and assign roles. A role needs <strong>access-admin</strong> plus the individual routes required for the work. Form pages and their save actions have separate permissions; some actions remain restricted to super administrators.</p><p>Volunteer accounts can be approved, but record-assignment restrictions are not yet enforced. Their role permissions may allow access to all records in a permitted area, so review those permissions carefully. Historical team entries do not automatically become accounts; a super administrator must create or explicitly link one after confirming identity.</p></section>
    <section id="guide-reports" class="admin-form-card admin-form-section"><h2>9. Filters, exports and installation</h2><p>Use table filters to narrow results. Check whether an export covers all matching records or only the current page. CSV files can be opened in Excel. Where supported, use Install app or the browser’s installation option. A computer’s 127.0.0.1 address is not reachable from another phone.</p></section>
    <section id="guide-therapy" class="admin-form-card admin-form-section"><h2>10. Children’s therapy</h2><p>Open Children’s therapy → Children, choose Register child and search the People registry by name or phone. Select an existing person or, if the child is not listed and you have permission, enter their first and last names. A guardian’s phone may be shared by siblings.</p><p>Complete the registration in steps or full view. Record each consent purpose separately and keep supporting documents private. From the child’s record, choose Record visit and select all services involved. Visit reports distinguish completed visits from missed or cancelled visits.</p><p>Therapy settings control services and registration options. Individual record assignments are not currently enforced; review staff access carefully.</p></section>
</div>
